WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
There was only one thing that made Patrasche uneasy.

2
00:00:05.521 --> 00:00:06.938
It was this:

3
00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:11.482
Nello often left Patrasche alone in the street.

4
00:00:11.483 --> 00:00:17.068
Antwerp, as all the world knows, is full of old churches.

5
00:00:17.069 --> 00:00:20.583
Nello loved to visit them.

6
00:00:20.584 --> 00:00:27.444
Antwerp's churches are jammed in everywhere, in almost every alley and street.

7
00:00:27.445 --> 00:00:32.469
Its churches are quiet, grand, old places of the past.

8
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:36.767
They are dark, ancient, and beautiful.

9
00:00:36.768 --> 00:00:46.773
Many of the churches contain the art of Antwerp's most beloved citizen: the great painter Peter Paul Rubens.

10
00:00:46.774 --> 00:00:54.039
Rubens was born in Flanders in 1577 and grew up in Antwerp.

11
00:00:54.040 --> 00:01:00.601
By the age of twenty-one, he was already an excellent painter.

12
00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:08.012
Rubens left Antwerp and, like other great painters of the time, he went to Italy.

13
00:01:08.013 --> 00:01:14.763
In Italy, he worked as a court painter and painted altars of churches in Rome.

14
00:01:14.764 --> 00:01:21.851
His works are famous for their color, their light, and their feeling of energy.

15
00:01:21.852 --> 00:01:29.937
In 1608, Rubens returned to Antwerp, where he continued to paint for many years.

16
00:01:29.938 --> 00:01:36.236
His paintings have religious themes and decorate its many ancient churches.

17
00:01:36.237 --> 00:01:41.534
In one of Antwerp's churches lies Rubens' tomb.

18
00:01:41.535 --> 00:01:45.215
Without Rubens, what is Antwerp?

19
00:01:45.216 --> 00:01:48.967
Merely a dirty, bustling market city.

20
00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:54.295
But because Rubens lived and worked there, Antwerp is sacred.

21
00:01:54.296 --> 00:02:00.286
Both worshippers of God and lovers of art honor its soil.

22
00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:09.191
Some afternoons, after Nello and Patrasche finished delivering the milk, Nello would stop outside a church.

23
00:02:09.192 --> 00:02:14.065
He would tell Patrasche to wait outside while he went in.

24
00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:19.318
Most often, he visited Antwerp's great cathedral.

25
00:02:19.319 --> 00:02:23.423
Once or twice, Patrasche tried to follow.

26
00:02:23.424 --> 00:02:32.538
He stepped through the cathedral's large gate, pulling his milk-cart behind, but a guard always sent him back.

27
00:02:32.539 --> 00:02:39.900
He waited on the street stones outside the iron gate and watched the people go by.

28
00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:44.639
"What does Nello do inside?" wondered Patrasche.

29
00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.831
"Sometimes he is inside for more than one hour!"

30
00:02:48.832 --> 00:02:57.214
Patrasche worried whenever Nello disappeared inside a church or went into the cathedral.

31
00:02:57.215 --> 00:03:02.828
Patrasche wasn't bothered just because Nello visited churches.

32
00:03:02.829 --> 00:03:07.534
Patrasche knew it was normal for people to go to church.

33
00:03:07.535 --> 00:03:15.856
After all, the farmers in their village went to the small gray church opposite the red windmill.

34
00:03:15.857 --> 00:03:22.413
Patrasche was worried because Nello always looked pale, when he came out.

35
00:03:22.414 --> 00:03:26.144
Nello was usually a talkative boy.

36
00:03:26.145 --> 00:03:33.450
But whenever he visited the cathedral, he would stay silent for hours after.

37
00:03:33.451 --> 00:03:40.036
If Nello visited the cathedral, when they returned home he never wanted to play.

38
00:03:40.037 --> 00:03:44.941
Instead, he would sit and gaze at the evening skies.

39
00:03:44.942 --> 00:03:50.478
Patrasche thought the little boy should not be so serious.

40
00:03:50.479 --> 00:03:55.497
But Nello kept visiting the cathedral and the churches.

41
00:03:55.498 --> 00:03:59.982
Patrasche could do nothing except wait in the street.

42
00:03:59.983 --> 00:04:06.443
He stretched himself out on the stones, yawned, and sighed.

43
00:04:06.444 --> 00:04:13.708
When Nello came out of the cathedral, he always hugged Patrasche and kissed his forehead.

44
00:04:13.709 --> 00:04:19.854
In a soft voice, he would murmur, "If I could only see them, Patrasche!"

45
00:04:19.855 --> 00:04:27.199
"See what?" wondered Patrasche.

